\p{I am a PhD student at the [[umich]] as part of the [Electrical and Computer Engineering program](https://ece.engin.umich.edu/), where my work #{\in} {programming languages} #{\cap} {computer architecture} #{\cap} {LLMs} #{\cap} {reinforcement learning}. I am co-advised by [[xinyuwang]] and [[satishnarayanasamy]]. Currently, \mark{I am interested in automated kernel generation across accelerators backends. In particular, neurosymbolic approaches to preserve guarantees and limit costs}. With this, I am looking into {[kernel DSLs](5PSC), [[IR7B]], [formal synthesis](Q30B), LLM "[vibe compilers](AV36)"}. I am also recreationally interested in Unix (see my [dotfiles](https://github.com/kkanarios32/dotfiles)) and in a past life I did research in [reinforcement learning algorithms](bib).
}
\p{I earned my BS in Mathematics and Computer Science from the [[umich]], graduating with honors and high honors, followed by an MS in [Electrical and Computer Engineering](https://ece.engin.umich.edu/). During this time, I was fortunate enough to be advised by [[leiying]]. My resume is available \<html:a>[style]{text-decoration: underline;}[href]{\route-asset{assets/files/kellen-kanarios-resume.pdf}}{here}. 
}

%\p{Previously, I obtained a BS from the [[umich]] in Mathematics and Computer Science, where I graduated with honors and high honors respectively. I also obtained my MS in Electrical and Computer Engineering from the [[umich]]. Across my undergrad and masters, I spent a wonderful 4ish years working with [[leiying]] in many facets, including as part of the [SURE Program](https://sure.engin.umich.edu/), as a TA for [EECS 602](https://sites.google.com/view/intro-to-rl/home), as a GSRA, and as a GSI for [ECE 567](https://bulletin.engin.umich.edu/courses/eecs/). 
%}

